' record as Atlanta mayor during the 2020 unrest, while Bottoms says the attacks distort her record.","src":"https://www.ajc.com/politics/2026/10/secoriea-turner-family-condemns-rick-jackson-ad/"},{"issue":"Health care and Medicaid","why":"Bottoms wants full Medicaid expansion and says Jackson profited from a broken health system, while Jackson backs a state waiver with work requirements.","src":"https://www.atlantanewsfirst.com/2026/09/17/bottoms-airs-first-true-attack-ad-linking-jackson-rigged-system/"},{"issue":"Data centers","why":"Bottoms calls for a pause on new data centers and questions Jackson's investments, while Jackson notes she approved a Midtown project with incentives.","src":"https://www.ajc.com/politics/2026/10/georgia-governors-race-follow-along-as-the-candidates-debate-on-tuesday/"},{"issue":"Affordability and taxes","why":"Jackson says voters care about gas prices, bills and property taxes, while Bottoms pledges to repeal the state grocery tax.","src":"https://www.wabe.org/bottoms-faces-empty-podium-on-debate-stage-while-jackson-campaigns-with-kemp/"},{"issue":"Abortion","why":"Bottoms used the debate he skipped to press Jackson on how rape exceptions work under Georgia's six week ban, which his campaign says mischaracterizes him.","src":"https://www.wabe.org/bottoms-faces-empty-podium-on-debate-stage-while-jackson-campaigns-with-kemp/"}],"storylines":[{"title":"Bottoms reports 23 million dollar haul","date":"2026-10-22","what":"Bottoms raised 23.2 million dollars since August with big DGA help, though Jackson has bought 87 million dollars in general election airtime from mostly his own money.","helps":"mixed","kind":"national","src":"https://www.ajc.com/politics/2026/10/keisha-lance-bottoms-fundraising/"},{"title":"AJC poll finds a dead heat","date":"2026-10-20","what":"Jackson led 46 to 45 among likely voters, with Bottoms ahead among independents and Democrats far more enthusiastic than Republicans.","helps":"mixed","kind":"national","src":"ht